Linuxtrack 1.3.7 (2026-03-11)
=============================

- Fixed a TrackIR regression introduced during webcam blob-threshold work by
  scoping blob-area scaling to webcam-style callers instead of the shared blob
  extractor.
- Added regression coverage for shared blob extraction semantics so webcam
  threshold tuning does not silently change TrackIR behavior again.
- Improved neural webcam face tracking with a configurable camera FOV, better
  pose holdover and filtering, restored translation scale, and stronger forward
  translation.
- Tuned several GUI tracking sliders so their useful range is less bunched and
  the labels match the actual smoothing behavior.
- Fixed the non-ONNX facetracker build so release jobs without ONNX support do
  not fail in `facetrack.cpp`.
- Repaired the AppImage/release path after the packaging work: the AppImage
  scripts now resolve the installed icon path dynamically, the release workflow
  installs X-Plane SDK headers so `xlinuxtrack9.so` is built into release
  artifacts again, and CI now uses the vendored Catch2 test sources.
- Updated GitHub Actions workflow dependencies to current Node 24-compatible
  lines and opted the workflows into Node 24 execution for JavaScript actions.
